  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: ouxinfo\n  version: \"1.1.3\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/${{ name[0] }}/${{ name }}/${{ name }}-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 35180890072d7307b938f43b7e3605fca255b4f5a8cf1bc1cef3a9921d65924e\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - setuptools\n    - pybind11\n    - if: linux\n      then: libgomp\n    - if: osx\n      then: llvm-openmp\n  run:\n    - python\n    - numpy\n    - matplotlib-base\n    - scipy\n    - tqdm\n    - joblib\n    - if: osx\n      then: llvm-openmp\n    - if: linux\n      then: libgomp\n    - if: win\n      then: vcomp14\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - ouxinfo\n      pip_check: true\n\nabout:\n  summary: Fast Shannon entropy estimator for causal inference in dynamical systems\n  description: |\n    OUxInfo is a high-performance Shannon entropy estimator for Python with a C++\n    backend. It implements k-nearest-neighbor (KSG/Kozachenko-Leonenko) algorithms\n    with a Chebyshev-metric k-d tree and OpenMP parallelization. Designed for\n    information-theoretic causal inference: transfer entropy, mutual information,\n    information flow, and KL divergence.\n  license: MIT AND BSD-2-Clause AND BSL-1.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - third_party/nanoflann/LICENSE\n    - third_party/boost/LICENSE_1_0.txt\n  homepage: https://github.com/htymjun/OUxInfo\n  repository: https://github.com/htymjun/OUxInfo\n  documentation: https://htymjun.github.io/OUxInfo\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - htymjun\n",
